{# Charmed PostgreSQL release notes template.

   Reproduces the structure of the product's published release notes, most
   recently VM revisions 1157/1158 and K8s revisions 926/927:
   https://canonical-charmed-postgresql-single-kernel.readthedocs-hosted.com/16/release-notes/
   source: canonical/postgresql-single-kernel-library, branch 16/docs,
           docs/release-notes/vm/1157-1158.md and docs/release-notes/k8s/926-927.md

   Differences from base.md.j2, and why:
   - MyST frontmatter with `html_meta.description` and a `(rev-NNNN-NNNN)=`
     anchor, as the docs build requires (the newest VM page 1157-1158.md lacks
     the frontmatter block — that is a gap in that file, not a convention;
     1088-1089.md and 926-927.md both carry it). The frontmatter must end up
     on line 1 of the saved file: if a review-notes HTML comment is added, it
     goes AFTER the frontmatter block. Otherwise Sphinx parses the `---`
     fences as body transitions and warns "Document headings start at H2, not
     H1".
   - Title is `# Revisions N, M` — the per-architecture revision pair, higher
     number first (the docs site supplies the product name via the `{{vm}}` /
     `{{k8s}}` substitution, which the docs build resolves; keep it verbatim
     on the line after the title).
   - No date line: none of the product's release-notes pages show a date.
   - Intro links use a MyST `{card}` directive with `{ref}` cross-references
     (`system-requirements`, `deploy`, `How to upgrade <refresh>`, and the
     per-charm index `release-notes-vm` / `release-notes-k8s`), not absolute
     URLs.
   - Compatibility table comes FIRST (before the changelog), with columns
     Architecture / Charm revision / Snap version (VM) or OCI image (K8s) /
     PostgreSQL version / Recommended Juju version, and a link-reference
     definition for the Juju version. The agent fills it per charm — the
     builder's generic table is not used.
   - Category headings render at `##` and the product uses its own section
     names: "Highlights" (hand-picked headline entries), then DA186-style
     "Features" / "Other features and improvements" / "Bug fixes". Map the
     builder's "Other improvements" to "Other features and improvements".
   - Entries use `* ` bullets, wrap Jira IDs in square brackets, and link the
     PR inline as `in {octicon}`mark-github` [#N](url)` — no `([PR \#N](url))`
     suffix, no commit link.
   - The product's pages end with a "New Contributors" section and a
     "Full Changelog" compare link; the agent adds these in the polish pass
     (the builder cannot know contributor firsts).
#}
{% extends "base.md.j2" %}

{% block frontmatter %}
---
myst:
  html_meta:
    description: "Release notes for Charmed PostgreSQL {{ title }}, TODO: one-sentence summary of the headline changes."
---

(rev-{{ title | lower | replace(" ", "-") | replace(",", "") }})=
{% endblock %}

{% block date_line %}{% endblock %}

{% block title %}
# {{ title }}
{{ component_subst }}
{% endblock %}

{% block introduction %}

<!-- TODO: Write a brief summary of the most important changes in this release. -->

{% block intro_links %}
```{card}
:text-align: center

[Charmhub]({{ charmhub_url }}) • {ref}`system-requirements` • {ref}`deploy` • {ref}`How to upgrade <refresh>` • {ref}`All release notes <{{ release_notes_ref }}>`
```
{% endblock %}
{% endblock %}

{% block changelog %}
{% for category in category_order %}
{% if categories.get(category) %}

## {{ category }}

{% for entry in categories[category] %}
* {% if entry.jira_ids %}{% for jira in entry.jira_ids %}[{{ jira }}](https://warthogs.atlassian.net/browse/{{ jira }}){% endfor %} {% endif %}{{ entry.message }}{% if entry.pr_number %} in {octicon}`mark-github` [#{{ entry.pr_number }}]({{ entry.pr_url }}){% endif %}

{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endblock %}

{% block compatibility %}
<!-- TODO: The agent fills the product's own compatibility table here
     (Architecture / Charm revision / Snap or OCI version / PostgreSQL
     version / Recommended Juju version), placed BEFORE the changelog. -->
{% endblock %}